---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const contactEmail = "privacy@owlfoundry.org";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | OwlFoundry"
  description="Terms governing access to OwlFoundry websites and hosted online services."
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="legal-effective-date">Effective August 6, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-content">
      <p>
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of the
        websites and hosted online services provided by OwlFoundry
        ("OwlFoundry," "we," "us," or "our") that link to these Terms
        (collectively, the "Services"). By using the Services, you agree to
        these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Services.
      </p>

      <section aria-labelledby="eligibility">
        <h2 id="eligibility">Eligibility</h2>
        <p>
          You must be legally capable of entering into these Terms. If you use
          the Services on behalf of an organization, you represent that you have
          authority to bind that organization, and "you" includes the
          organization.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="accounts">
        <h2 id="accounts">Accounts and authentication</h2>
        <p>
          Some Services may require an account or allow you to authenticate with
          Google or another third-party identity provider. You are responsible
          for keeping your account secure, for maintaining accurate account
          information, and for activity conducted through your account. Notify
          us promptly if you suspect unauthorized use.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your use of a third-party identity provider is also governed by that
          provider's terms and privacy practices.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="acceptable-use">
        <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You may not use the Services to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>violate applicable law or the rights of others;</li>
          <li>distribute malware or facilitate phishing, fraud, or abuse;</li>
          <li>
            gain or attempt to gain unauthorized access to accounts, systems, or
            data;
          </li>
          <li>
            disrupt, overload, probe, scan, or test the vulnerability of the
            Services except with our prior written permission;
          </li>
          <li>
            evade usage limits, security controls, or access restrictions; or
          </li>
          <li>
            use the Services in a way that materially interferes with other
            users' use of them.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="your-content">
        <h2 id="your-content">Your content</h2>
        <p>
          You retain ownership of content you submit to the Services. You grant
          us a limited, worldwide, non-exclusive license to host, copy, process,
          transmit, and display that content only as reasonably necessary to
          provide, secure, and improve the Services or comply with law. You are
          responsible for your content and must have the rights needed to
          provide it to us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="open-source-software">
        <h2 id="open-source-software">Open-source software</h2>
        <p>
          Software we publish under an open-source license is governed by the
          applicable license and repository documentation, not these Terms.
          These Terms apply to OwlFoundry-operated websites and hosted services;
          they do not govern third-party or self-hosted deployments of our
          open-source software.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="our-rights">
        <h2 id="our-rights">Our rights</h2>
        <p>
          The Services, including their design, branding, and content provided
          by us, are owned by OwlFoundry or its licensors and are protected by
          applicable intellectual property laws. Except for rights expressly
          granted under these Terms or an open-source license, we reserve all
          rights.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="third-party-services">
        <h2 id="third-party-services">Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The Services may link to or interoperate with third-party services. We
          do not control those services and are not responsible for their
          content, availability, or practices. Your use of third-party services
          is governed by their own terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="service-changes">
        <h2 id="service-changes">Service changes and availability</h2>
        <p>
          We may modify, suspend, or discontinue any part of the Services. We do
          not guarantee that the Services will always be available,
          uninterrupted, secure, or error-free. We may establish or change
          reasonable usage limits to protect the Services and their users.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="termination">
        <h2 id="termination">Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>
          You may stop using the Services at any time. We may suspend or
          terminate access if you materially breach these Terms, create security
          or legal risk, fail to pay applicable fees, or if continued access
          would harm the Services or others. Where reasonably practicable, we
          will provide notice and an opportunity to resolve the issue.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="disclaimers">
        <h2 id="disclaimers">Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Services are provided "as
          is" and "as available." OwlFoundry disclaims all warranties, express
          or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a
          particular purpose, non-infringement, and any warranties arising from
          course of dealing or usage of trade. Nothing in these Terms excludes a
          warranty that cannot lawfully be excluded.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="limitation-of-liability">
        <h2 id="limitation-of-liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, OwlFoundry and its
          contributors, affiliates, and service providers will not be liable for
          indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive
          damages, or for lost profits, revenues, data, goodwill, or business
          opportunities, arising from or related to the Services or these Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, OwlFoundry's total liability
          for all claims arising from or related to the Services or these Terms
          will not exceed the greater of the amount you paid us for the Services
          during the 12 months before the event giving rise to the claim or
          US$100. These limitations do not apply where prohibited by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="changes-to-terms">
        <h2 id="changes-to-terms">Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. We will publish the
          updated Terms on this page and revise the effective date. If a change
          is material, we will provide additional notice when reasonably
          practicable. Your continued use of the Services after updated Terms
          take effect means you accept them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="general">
        <h2 id="general">General</h2>
        <p>
          If any provision of these Terms is held unenforceable, the remaining
          provisions will remain in effect. Our failure to enforce a provision
          is not a waiver. You may not transfer these Terms without our consent.
          We may transfer them as part of a reorganization, merger, acquisition,
          or sale of assets. These Terms, together with any service-specific
          terms, form the entire agreement between you and OwlFoundry regarding
          the Services.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contact-us">
        <h2 id="contact-us">Contact us</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms may be sent to
          <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
